       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the usual maximum adult dose of 10 mg once daily. Even with normal kidney and liver function, that dose could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. In overdose it can cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nWas this a typo? The usual dosing is:\n- **Starting dose:** 5 mg by mouth once daily. For frail or elderly patients, or those with hepatic impairment, it's 2.5 mg.\n- **Maximum dose:** 10 mg by mouth once daily.\n\nIf you meant 5 mg or 10 mg, tell me which and I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 50 mg, please confirm that and give me the clinical rationale. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
